---
import ProsePage from "../layouts/ProsePage.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy";
const description =
  "Blankie's privacy policy: Blankie collects no personal data, runs no analytics or tracking and works 100% offline on Mac, iPhone, iPad and CarPlay.";
---

<ProsePage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  meta="Effective Oct. 28, 2026"
>
  <div class="markdown-alert">
    <p class="markdown-alert-title">A note from Blankie's creator</p>
    <p>I wrote this privacy policy because Apple made me, but I'm glad I did, because you deserve to know exactly what an app does with your data. Blankie does nothing with your data because it never asks for it, and with nothing to sell, it has nothing to hide.</p>
    <p>Making money off people's data is gross, so Blankie doesn't do it. The only servers Blankie talks to are Apple's, just to download animated artwork. If you do ever choose to share something with me, I'll use what you share for the purposes you intended. The rest of the text below says all of this in more specific, legal language, but hopefully you get the idea.</p>
  </div>

  <p>This privacy policy applies only to the Blankie app and this website, not to any third-party services or websites they may link to. By using the app or this website, you agree to the terms of this policy. If you do not agree, please do not use them.</p>

  <h2>Data Collection</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No Data Collection in App</strong>: The Blankie app never asks for, stores or sends us any personal data such as names, emails or physical addresses, whether you download it from this website, GitHub, Homebrew or an Apple platform. Any usage statistics we receive come solely from Apple.</li>
    <li><strong>No Analytics or Trackers</strong>: Neither the official Blankie app nor this website uses trackers, advertising networks, analytics frameworks or any other third-party services, libraries, SDKs or APIs that collect personal data.</li>
    <li><strong>Website Logs</strong>: To detect attacks and abusive bots, this website logs the page, response status, country, network and bot score of each request. These logs never contain your IP address, browser, device or any location more precise than your country, so they cannot identify you. They are deleted automatically within seven days.</li>
    <li><strong>Information You Provide</strong>: If you email us, send feedback through our form or TestFlight, support Blankie on Ko-fi or Buy Me a Coffee, or contribute code or translations, we receive whatever you choose to share, such as your name or email address. We use it only to reply to you, credit you or contact you about your contribution, and we will never sell it or use it for any other purpose. You do not need to share your name or email address with us to contribute to the project (communicating publicly via GitHub issues and discussions is actually our preference).</li>
    <li><strong>Third Parties</strong>: Platform providers like Apple, GitHub and Homebrew may collect some anonymous usage data when you use their platforms and services to interact with the Blankie project or download Blankie. In most cases we cannot access this data or control how these platforms use it, so we recommend reviewing their privacy policies. This website is hosted by Cloudflare, which processes IP addresses to deliver and secure it under the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Apple and TestFlight</h2>
  <p>Apple provides app developers with limited, anonymized analytics about how many people download an app and in which countries. Your iPhone, iPad or Mac also has a setting called <b>Share With App Developers</b>, which you may have turned on when you first set it up. If it's on, Apple can also send developers anonymous crash reports and usage data, such as how often the app is opened and if you start using it again after a period of time. At no point does Apple ever tell us who you are. We use information from Apple only to make Blankie more stable and reliable. To opt out of sharing anonymous crash reports and usage data, open your device's Settings app (not Blankie's settings) and go to <b>Privacy &amp; Security → Analytics &amp; Improvements</b>. You can learn more about Apple's data collection practices in the <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/data/en/app-store/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">App Store Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

  <p>When you send feedback through our public TestFlight beta, Apple shares it with us along with details about your device. If you joined through our public link, your name and email stay hidden unless you add your email to the feedback. We never receive anything that identifies you unless you choose to share it.</p>

  <p>Trusted contributors may occasionally be invited to private TestFlight betas. To send the invitation, we must give the contributor's email address to Apple. We will use it only to facilitate the invitation and will never share it with anyone else or use it for any purpose beyond what the contributor has consented to.</p>

  <h2>Data Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
  <p>We never sell personal information or share it beyond what this policy describes.</p>

  <h2>Official Downloads</h2>
  <p>The App Store, blankie.rest (this website), Homebrew, GitHub and TestFlight are Blankie's official distribution channels. We cannot guarantee that copies from any other source are safe or secure. Blankie is open source and you can always build it from source if you want to verify the code yourself. If you do this, you are responsible for your own privacy and security. However you get it, Blankie is provided "as is," without warranty of any kind, as stated in its <a href="https://github.com/codybrom/blankie/blob/main/LICENSE">open-source license</a>.</p>

  <h2>Updates to this Policy</h2>
  <p>Apple's developer requirements and other legal standards may evolve. If we update this policy to reflect such changes, you'll find the latest version here. Our commitment to privacy won't change.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>For questions or concerns regarding this policy, email <a href="mailto:info@blankie.rest">info@blankie.rest</a> or open a <a href="https://github.com/codybrom/blankie/issues">GitHub Issue</a>.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Oct. 28, 2026: Named Cloudflare as this website's host, disclosed the anonymous logs it keeps to detect abuse, listed the ways you can share information with us, explained Apple's Share With App Developers setting and TestFlight feedback, and added the no-warranty notice.</li>
    <li>June 7, 2026: Changed "Mac App Store" to "App Store" now that Blankie is also available on iOS and iPadOS.</li>
    <li>May 15, 2025: Initial version of the privacy policy.</li>
  </ul>
</ProsePage>
